ew" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKASU TOSHIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANDO, MITURU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MUROI, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGURI, KAZUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKASU, TOSHIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A continuous casting nozzle for molten steel, wherein a nozzle inner hole surface layer, in contact with the molten steel, of the continuous casting nozzle is obtained by adding, before kneading and molding, a binder to Al2O3 or a composition consisting of Al2O3 as a main component, 15 to 60 wt. % of an aggregate having a melting temperature of not lower than 1800  DEG C and agalmatolite as the remaining part, and firing the molded product in a non-oxidizing atmosphere.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une tuyère destinée à la coulée en continu d'acier en fusion, dans laquelle on obtient un revêtement intérieur perforé, au contact de l'acier en fusion, par addition, préalablement au brassage et au moulage, d'un liant de Al2O3 ou d'une composition renfermant Al2O3 comme composant principal, de 15 à 60 % en poids d'un agrégat ayant une température de fusion supérieure ou égale à 1800  DEG C, et pour le reste, d'agalmatolite ; puis par cuisson du produit moulé dans une atmosphère non oxydante.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires